{"id": "SGU_Episode_632", "title": "SGU Episode 632", "type": "structured", "description": "The Skeptic's Guide to the Universe, Episode 632 Transcript", "metadata": {"title": "SGU Episode 632", "date": "August 19 2024", "year": 2024, "month": 8, "day": 19, "rogues": ["Steven Novella", "Jay Novella", "Evan Bernstein", "Bob Novella", "Cara Santa Maria"], "quotee_url": "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jocelyn_Bell_Burnell", "quote": "\n Science doesn't always go forwards. It's a bit like doing a Rubik's cube. You sometimes have to make more of a mess with a Rubik's cube before you can get it to go right. \n", "quotee": "\n Jocelyn Bell Burnell \n", "quotee_title": "", "categories": [], "podcast_url": "https://www.theskepticsguide.org/podcasts/episode-632", "episode_number": 632}, "sections": [{"id": 0, "text": "You're listening to the Skeptics' Guide to the Universe, your escape to reality.\n", "title": "Introduction", "metadata": {"title": "Introduction"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 1, "text": "Eclipse Terminology", "title": "What's the Word", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "What's the Word"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 2, "text": "", "title": "News Items", "metadata": {"title": "News Items"}, "sections": [{"id": 3, "text": "http://interestingengineering.com/concrete-gravity-trains-may-solve-energy-storage-problem/", "title": "Concrete Gravity Trains", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "links": ["http://interestingengineering.com/concrete-gravity-trains-may-solve-energy-storage-problem/"], "title": "Concrete Gravity Trains"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 4, "text": "http://theness.com/neurologicablog/index.php/more-on-the-backfire-effect/", "title": "Backfire Effect", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "links": ["http://theness.com/neurologicablog/index.php/more-on-the-backfire-effect/"], "title": "Backfire Effect"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 5, "text": "http://www.bbc.com/news/health-40925343", "title": "Polio Vaccine from Tobacco", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "links": ["http://www.bbc.com/news/health-40925343"], "title": "Polio Vaccine from Tobacco"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 6, "text": "https://www.sciencealert.com/the-science-world-s-freaking-out-over-this-25-year-old-s-solution-to-antibiotic-resistance", "title": "Antibiotic Resistance", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "links": ["https://www.sciencealert.com/the-science-world-s-freaking-out-over-this-25-year-old-s-solution-to-antibiotic-resistance"], "title": "Antibiotic Resistance"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 7, "text": "https://sciencebasedmedicine.org/alternative-medicine-kills-cancer-patients/", "title": "Alternative Medicine Kills", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "links": ["https://sciencebasedmedicine.org/alternative-medicine-kills-cancer-patients/"], "title": "Alternative Medicine Kills"}, "sections": []}]}, {"id": 8, "text": "Answer to last week: VODER", "title": "Who's That Noisy", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "Who's That Noisy"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 9, "text": "", "title": "Questions and Emails", "metadata": {"title": "Questions and Emails"}, "sections": [{"id": 10, "text": "", "title": "Atheist Study Follow Up", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "Atheist Study Follow Up"}, "sections": [{"id": 11, "text": "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41562-017-0151", "metadata": {"links": ["https://www.nature.com/articles/s41562-017-0151"], "speaker": "<unknown>"}}]}]}, {"id": 12, "text": "Item #1: Scientists have developed a technique for imaging subjective pain intensity using electroencephalogram.\nItem #2: Scientists have developed a technique for imaging nerves intraoperatively using only polarized light with 100% accuracy.\nItem #3: Researchers have developed a new MRI scan technique that allows for imaging in two colors at once.\n", "title": "Science or Fiction", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "Science or Fiction"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 13, "text": "", "title": "Skeptical Quote of the Week", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "Skeptical Quote of the Week"}, "sections": [{"id": 14, "text": "\u201cScience doesn't always go forwards. It's a bit like doing a Rubik's cube. You sometimes have to make more of a mess with a Rubik's cube before you can get it to go right.\u201d - Jocelyn Bell Burnell", "metadata": {"speaker": "<unknown>"}}, {"id": 15, "text": "The Skeptics' Guide to the Universe is produced by SGU Productions, dedicated to promoting science and critical thinking. For more information on this and other episodes, please visit our website at theskepticsguide.org, where you will find the show notes as well as links to our blogs, videos, online forum, and other content. You can send us feedback or questions to info@theskepticsguide.org. Also, please consider supporting the SGU by visiting the store page on our website, where you will find merchandise, premium content, and subscription information. Our listeners are what make SGU possible.", "metadata": {"links": ["http://www.theskepticsguide.org", "https://www.theskepticsguide.org/shop"], "speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}]}, {"id": 16, "text": "", "title": "References", "metadata": {"title": "References"}, "sections": []}]}